      {
        "id": 99521,
        "name": "Matchstickman",
        "username": "Matchstickman",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/matchstickman/{size}/1880_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-04-16T22:37:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>No, it's talking about resolving effects still 'in action'.</p><p>The effect of Galvanize for example has already resolved. It has already added one to hero damage until the start of Legacy's next turn.</p><p>If a Citizen is dealing damage to all hero targets and you let Ra take the first hit, Ra can hit it with Flame Barrier and kill the Citizen, the effect (dealing damage to all hero targets) is canceled as the card is destroyed mid-effect.</p>",
        "post_number": 9,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:27:31.161Z",
